2026-09-02T15:53:19.936Z|01518|connmgr|INFO|s1<->tcp:127.0.0.1:6653: sending OFPMMFC_UNKNOWN_METER error reply to OFPST_METER_CONFIG request message
  ^ these are UNKNOWN_METER replies to OFPST_METER_CONFIG *stats requests* -- the existence
    check asking about a meter that was already gone. NOT meter_mod errors: no METER_MOD was
    ever rejected, which is why meter deletes worked and group deletes did not.

== reading ==
  The delete DID reach the switch. It was REJECTED, with OFPGMFC_INVALID_GROUP, and because
  Ryu sends the group_mod with no barrier and awaits no reply (ofctl_v1_3.py:1151) it had
  already answered 200 before the rejection arrived, correlated to nothing.
  OFPGMFC_INVALID_GROUP is not what OF1.3 gives for deleting a group that is not there --
  that is a silent no-op at the switch. It is a validation refusal of the message itself.
  Group ids in play were 88/555/601/602/603, far below OFPG_MAX, so an out-of-range id is
  excluded. The remaining candidate is the bucket list: the caller's install-shaped body
  was forwarded verbatim as the delete, and OFPGC_DELETE gives buckets no meaning.
  ⚠️ That last step is INFERENCE, not measurement. The live A/B that settles it is section 6
     of scratchpad/live_arm.sh: same id, delete-with-buckets vs delete-minimal, both driven
     straight at Ryu so the kernel is not a variable.
